 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/DbuOOvRSeQJ/",
 "title": "Build a Recognisable Personal Brand Through Intentional Pairings",
 "topic": "content creation",
 "summary": "The creator explains that personal branding is about intentionally and consistently pairing yourself with specific ideas, people, and objects. Using creator Shelby Sapp as an example, the lesson is to be deliberate about what you associate with—and what you avoid associating with—to build a recognizable brand.",
 "key_points": [
  "Branding definition by Caleb Ralston: Branding is the process of intentionally pairing yourself with the right people, ideas, and values, and doing it consistently.",
  "Personal brand definition: The pairing of things with yourself repeatedly.",
  "Example of Shelby Sapp: She consistently pairs herself with pink cars (Rolls Royce, Porsche, G Wagon), her mansion, pilates, sales, and a hot girl bougie lifestyle.",
  "First lever: Be very intentional and consistent about what you pair yourself with to build a huge recognizable brand.",
  "Second lever: Be intentional about what you do NOT want to be paired with to avoid muddying your image.",
  "Action step: Think about what you want to be paired with and what you don't want to be paired with, and be deliberate."
 ],
 "content": "This guy is the content mastermind behind these two guys, and there's this one principle he teaches which she uses to dominate organic content. It's a simple principle I got from this video and it's about the definition of branding. Caleb defines a personal brand as the pairing of things with yourself repeatedly, like we pair Shelby with her pink Rolls Royce, her pink Porsche, her pink G Wagon, her mansion, and this hot girl bougie lifestyle. This is why she has such a huge recognizable brand. She's very intentional and very consistent about what she pairs herself with. These pairings and associations become your brand, which is why it's so important to be intentional about it. So have a think about what you want to be paired with and what you don't want to be paired with, and make sure you're being really deliberate. Follow for more breakdowns.",
